<!--
  Frère Jacques
  Are You Sleeping? Traditional French round (18th century). Public domain.
  C major, 4/4, quarter = 96, 16 bars: once in French, once in English (40 s).
  Right hand: the melody, G3-A4. Left hand: C3 and G3, and only C3 under the low G3 of
  "ding, dang, dong". Every note is in C3-B4.

  bar | right hand        | left hand | words
    1 | C4 D4 E4 C4       | C3 G3     | Frè-re Jac-ques,
    2 | C4 D4 E4 C4       | C3 G3     | Frè-re Jac-ques,
    3 | E4 F4 G4          | C3 G3     | dor-mez-vous?
    4 | E4 F4 G4          | C3 G3     | Dor-mez-vous?
    5 | G4 A4 G4 F4 E4 C4 | C3 G3     | Son-nez les ma-ti-nes,
    6 | G4 A4 G4 F4 E4 C4 | C3 G3     | son-nez les ma-ti-nes,
    7 | C4 G3 C4          | C3        | ding, dang, dong.
    8 | C4 G3 C4          | C3        | Ding, dang, dong.
    9 | C4 D4 E4 C4       | C3 G3     | Are you sleep-ing,
   10 | C4 D4 E4 C4       | C3 G3     | are you sleep-ing,
   11 | E4 F4 G4          | C3 G3     | Bro-ther John?
   12 | E4 F4 G4          | C3 G3     | Bro-ther John?
   13 | G4 A4 G4 F4 E4 C4 | C3 G3     | Morn-ing bells are ring-ing,
   14 | G4 A4 G4 F4 E4 C4 | C3 G3     | morn-ing bells are ring-ing,
   15 | C4 G3 C4          | C3        | ding, dang, dong.
   16 | C4 G3 C4          | C3        | Ding, dang, dong.
-->
